<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7874"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 4:37 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://ww2.kake.com/global/video/popup/pop_player" target=_top>http://ww2.kake.com/global/video/popup/pop_player</a>. asp?ClipID1=354575 <BR> <BR> <BR>IMO this video has som intense underlaying messages to BTK .  <BR>I wonder if the police now strongly suspect who BTK is and is showing him off in several of the clips in this video? I think so!  <BR>And I think BTK is from LE. <BR> <BR>The first thing I find strange is the capter 1. &#34;a serial killer is born&#34;.  <BR>In this part of the video they are showing clips of Lt. Kenneth Landwehr in slowmotion while talking about that BTK probably was traumazised as a cild, through this slowmotion clips of lt. Kenneth Landwehr they make hypershort clips of several of the murderscenes. That sequence is SO strange to me, it is as if they are talking about Kenneth Landwehr, and also indirectly sending a message &#34;we understand you, we know you was traumetized as a child come forward we want to help you&#34; if this is all wrong &#40;VERY likely&#41; they realy need som help editing their videos at KAKE because ther ARE telling a underlying story in this video wich implicates specific persons. <BR> <BR>Also I cant help wondering about Kenneth Landwehr´s problem with reading his statements at the newsconfereces &#40;he almost always have this problem&#41; to me he seems almost on the ege of not beeing able to go through with the statements, in several other videos &#40;not this one&#41; he stops for almost a second before he goes on and stumbles on the words ect. and I find that strange for a policeman who is chosen as the one to speak to the public. <BR> <BR>The destinct showing a huge Wichita Police badge at the end of the video also, to me, COULD mean &#34; we suspect BTK is a police officer&#34; <BR> <BR>The last thing, in the end of the video there is a sequence with the possible victime Delores. In that seqence they show the SAME clip 3, read THREE, times showing 4 policemen &#40;I presume&#41; carrying Dolores body. WHY SHOWING THIS CLIP 3 TIMES in 45 seconds??? And who are those police officers? is one of them Kenneth Landwehr? <BR> <BR>By the way I´m still VERY interested in the HOMO-CIDEman with dark hair and dark coat in the other video. <BR> to poster &#34;Whoisbtk&#34; where are you???  <BR>please give us an answer on who this man is, is it Frank Cummins? Do you know where to find a picture of him?  <BR> <BR>I have tried and the only thing I could find was this, he actually resemblece the man in the video but as I understand it, this websites is from ireland. Interesting is that the team he is playing on is called &#34;Railway Cup Hurling Champions&#34; the pictures is from 1973 and 1974. <BR> <BR><a href="http://216.239.59.104/search?q=cache:RAEsbGRWBdUJ:leinster.gaa.ie/photo_1970_1980s.htm%2B%22Railway%2BCup%2BHurling%2BChampions%2B%22%2B%2B%22frank%2Bcummins%22&amp;hl=en" target=_top>http://216.239.59.104/search?q=cache:RAEsbGRWBdUJ: leinster.gaa.ie/photo_1970_1980s.htm&#43;%22Railway&#43;Cu p&#43;Hurling&#43;Champions&#43;%22&#43;%2B%22frank&#43;cummins%22&amp;hl= en</a> &#40;this link with his name highlighted&#41; <BR> <BR><a href="http://leinster.gaa.ie/photo_1970_1980s.htm" target=_top>http://leinster.gaa.ie/photo_1970_1980s.htm</a> <BR>  <BR>1973 Railway Cup Hurling Champions - Leinster  <BR>Front Row &#40;l to r&#41; - Teddy O&#39;Connor, Jim Treacy, Noel Skehan, Pat Delaney &#40;capt.&#41;, Padraig Horan, Mick Mahon, Martin Quigley, Tony Doran,  <BR>Back Row &#40;l to r&#41; - Mick Bermingham, Kieran Purcell, Pat Lawlor, Mick Jacob, Frank Cummins, Eddie Keher, Pat Henderson  <BR>  <BR>1975 Railway Cup Hurling Champions - Leinster  <BR>Front Row &#40;l to r&#41; - Tony Doran, Pat Quigley, Mick Jacob, Pat Delaney &#40;capt.&#41;, Padraig Horan, Martin Quigley, Liam O&#39;Brien  <BR>Back Row &#40;l to r&#41; - Phil Larkin, Pat Lawlor, Kieran Purcell, Pat Henderson, Eddie Keher, Frank Cummins, Noel Skehan, Pat Dunny  <BR>  <BR> Also his lack of beeing willing to give DNA sample is VERY suspicious IMO, and yes the sugestion to take his fingerprits and compare with the one they have of BTK is a good idea IMO. <BR><a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/state/10240078.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/state/102400 78.htm</a> <BR>Request for police DNA in BTK investigation raising controversy <BR>  <BR><a href="http://66.102.9.104/search?q=cache:CKhr7sP1yTMJ:www.ksn.com/news/stories/6562988.html%2B%22Frank%2BCummins%22%2B%2Bbtk&amp;hl=en" target=_top>http://66.102.9.104/search?q=cache:CKhr7sP1yTMJ:ww w.ksn.com/news/stories/6562988.html&#43;%22Frank&#43;Cummi ns%22&#43;%2Bbtk&amp;hl=en</a> <BR>Why are BTK investigators asking their own for DNA samples? <BR>  <BR><a href="http://66.102.9.104/search?q=cache:i51pZ57ArHQJ:www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/unsolved/btk/15.html%3Fsect%3D4%2B%22Frank%2BCummins%22%2B%2Bbtk&amp;hl=en" target=_top>http://66.102.9.104/search?q=cache:i51pZ57ArHQJ:ww w.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/unsolved/btk/15. html%3Fsect%3D4&#43;%22Frank&#43;Cummins%22&#43;%2Bbtk&amp;hl=en</a> <BR>According to Roy Wenzl&#39;s November 21, 2004 article in the Wichita Eagle, retired Det. Frank Cummins was skeptical of the DNA tests because of long-term privacy concerns. Wenzl reported that &#34;because of the nature of DNA, because it can show genetic family relationships, it would be like handing the police department a permanent set of fingerprints, without permission from every person genetically related to him.&#34; Moreover, Cummins believed that the tests were a waste of money and he distrusted how the police would utilize the samples. Consequently, he decided not to voluntarily provide DNA samples. He would not be the last person to refuse police testing. <BR> <BR> Sorry for posting such a long post, but a last thing: <BR> <BR>Does anyone see/recognize a specific police officer in the vido added in this post who appears many times throughout the video? <BR> <BR>thanks<!--/Text--></td></tr>
