<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7893"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Topsailgrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Topsailgrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 6:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->OK, this is my take on the video.... <BR> <BR>Remember the video that showed and had a small segment on subliminals? Did you catch how many subliminals are in this video??? There are at least one for each chapter that they speak about and two quick flashes before they start going down the list of chapters. I could only catch a couple of them. Just not quick enough I guess. The ones that I did catch have white handwriting against the red background. I can hardly make the writing out but it&#39;s there! We need someone who can catch these things. There are so many of them! Check the video out again, really pay attention to it. Looks to me, that they were sending a message in the previous video about subliminals. Possibly letting BTK know that they were on the way or to be suggestive for future videos. I guarantee you that the FBI is working with Kake on this. <BR> <BR>Anyone who is good with computers and these videos please take a look and see what can be done with these. I think there are very very important clues here.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7893-->
<!--Post: 7897--><!--Time: 1108739707-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7897"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Surfietx<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Surfietx<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 7:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;ve got this phrase so far, &#34;time, but&#34; in the red writing of which you speak.  I&#39;m working on it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7897-->
<!--Post: 7898--><!--Time: 1108739841-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7898"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Surfietx<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Surfietx<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 7:17 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->How do you do a screen capture?  I have the first of the two quick flashes on my screen.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7898-->
<!--Post: 7899--><!--Time: 1108739948-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7899"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Surfietx<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Surfietx<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 7:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;ll start a new thread since this is off topic.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7899-->
<!--Post: 7903--><!--Time: 1108740354-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7903"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Topsailgrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Topsailgrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 7:25 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I could make out those two words also and the word you, but that&#39;s it. I wonder if the writing is BTK&#39;s own handwriting? <BR> <BR>Another thing is, most of the flashes are very quick and are of what appears to be old footage but they are soooooo fast that I really cant say for sure! It&#39;s driving me bonkers! Which goes to show you how good the power of suggestion works! I seriously think the previous video ABOUT subliminals IS the power of suggestion for future videos. Did that make sense??? LOL Remember, they kept hyping up the revealing of the chapters to the point that after being showed people were somewhat dissapointed and thought that it was done for ratings. I think the hype was to make sure that BTK&#39;s concentration level during the airing would be at a peak. I dont live in the area so I dont see the news out there and am now wondering how many of these subliminals/flashes have been used during advertising of the up comming news events about BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7903-->
<!--Post: 7976--><!--Time: 1108771353-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7976"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brown_tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brown_tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 4:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->KAKE had to get special permission from the FCC to do the subliminal thing. It&#39;s illigal to do sublim. messages anymore. So, it&#39;s not likely that any more sublims are happening now.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7976-->
<!--Post: 7988--><!--Time: 1108774113-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7988"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tadpole<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tadpole<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 4:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well, those clips may not have been meant to be subliminal but they sure weren&#39;t on screen long enough to see what they were!  They sure played with my mind!  LOL!  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7988-->
<!--Post: 7990--><!--Time: 1108774656-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7990"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bodycheck<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bodycheck<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 4:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->hmmm...hadnt even caught that the first time...let me see if i can get to teh video source and pull it down...then take it apart frame by frame....should be able to post images of those frames... <BR> <BR>stay tuned <BR> <BR>B<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7990-->
<!--Post: 7995--><!--Time: 1108778788-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7995"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brown_tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brown_tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 6:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->the message simply was this: <BR> <BR>a hand drawn pair of eyeglasses &#40;upside down&#41;, and the words: CALL THE CHIEF NOW written above the glasses<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7995-->
<!--Post: 7996--><!--Time: 1108780097-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7996"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:nugzter@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 6:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Why are there no pics of F. Cummins? Is he the invisible man? Someone must have old or new photos to compare to video.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7996-->
<!--Post: 7997--><!--Time: 1108780179-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7997"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Topsailgrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Topsailgrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 6:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Not that video Brown_tornado, check this thread and video and you will see what we are talking about. We moved the thread because it was getting off topic here <BR>Many more new subliminals here <BR> <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/10/525.html?1108770248" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/10/525.htm l?1108770248</a> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7997-->
<!--Post: 8031--><!--Time: 1108823864-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8031"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Surfietx<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Surfietx<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 19, 2005 - 6:37 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Look at the enhancements that Sara did in this thread - post number 41 in particular. <BR> <BR><a href="http://forums.prospero.com/foxamw/messages/?msg=1689.1" target=_top>http://forums.prospero.com/foxamw/messages/?msg=16 89.1</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8031-->
<!--Post: 8528--><!--Time: 1109185138-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8528"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hkenley@san.rr.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Chiefron<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiefron<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 10:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Using a commercially available forensic audio software package I compared the voices from the 911 call and the video provided.  <BR> <BR>I am not a professional and the program provides no way of conducting voice print matches unless you purchase the full thousand dollar package but it supplies everything needed to do manual matches. Assuming a large margin for error I conducted a slow frequency spectrum average on the areas of each audio file where the word homicide is spoken. I did no editing or cleaning of either file so expected a good deal of variance due to background noise in the 911 call as compared to the relatively clear audio from the video footage. Here is what I discovered: <BR> <BR>The slow average of the spectrum for the roughly 1 second of audio is almost an exact match with only slight variance across the entire spectrum of the human voice range. Both voices fall well within the human male frequency range and curiously enough have less than 2hz/db variance across the entire range for the word homicide.  <BR> <BR>The results from this were e-mailed to WPD on the 18th of February as a tip on their cold case in the hopes that WPD&#39;s forensic audio folks might see it as an avenue of investigation, obviously admitting the fact that I am not an expert and my analysis might be completely wrong. To the inexpert eye however the match is pretty compelling, I hope they look into it. <BR> <BR>Ron<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8528-->
<!--Post: 8535--><!--Time: 1109187729-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8535"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Topsailgrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Topsailgrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 11:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Facinating Chiefron! I too hope if it hasnt been looked into already it will be. Hey, it&#39;s just a good a lead as any I have seen so far if not better.  <BR> <BR>At the very least, this guy needs to be ruled out. Put personalities aside WPD, and do not discount that it could be one of your own, past or present.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8535-->
